Notebook[{
 Cell["Rotating heterotic to five-dimensional STU field map", "Title"],
 Cell["Exact raw reduction, corrected KK scalar, and a controlled conditional ledger", "Subtitle"],
 Cell["Purpose and scope", "Section"],
 Cell["This standalone notebook checks the part of the ten-dimensional heterotic string-frame to five-dimensional Einstein/Riemann-frame map that can be evaluated compactly. It works to first order in alphaPrime and is exact in the rotation parameter a. It intentionally does not label the corrected winding-vector, corrected dualization, or final component comparison as proved before their full tensor substitutions are performed.", "Text"],
 Cell["Conventions: x=r^2; (qplus,qminus,qzero) map to (mu1,mu2,mu3); a maps to j. To compare arXiv:2606.31987 with the local STU source, rewrite the metric in mostly-plus signature, reverse the circle coordinate z, and use H_STU=-H_2606. These choices give A1=Hplus^(-1) Theta, A2=Hminus^(-1) Theta, A3=Hzero^(-1) Theta at two derivatives.", "Text"],
 Cell["Dualization convention used by the completed certificates. The final source action has +C wedge (d h+F wedge G), while the physical third potential remains A3=+Hzero^(-1) Theta as in Eq. (4.1). The flat-index symbol has epsilonLower[0,1,2,3,4]=+1 and epsilonUpper[0,1,2,3,4]=-1; the curved tensor used in the Hodge map is its five-vielbein transform. Together with star5^2=-1 on Lorentzian three-forms, these choices require h=-Exp[2 Phi] star5 F3+(alphaPrime/8) J. The sign multiplying J remains positive. Notebook 23 checks the relation componentwise; the numerical sector proved in this notebook is unaffected.", "Text"],

 Cell["1. Corrected profiles in concise notation", "Section"],
 Cell[BoxData["ClearAll[\"Global`*\"]; $HistoryLength = 0;\n$Assumptions = x > 0 && r > 0 && qplus > 0 && qminus > 0 && qzero > 0 && Element[{a, alphaPrime}, Reals];\n\nhplus = 1 + qplus/x;\nhminus = 1 + qminus/x;\nhzero = 1 + qzero/x;\nw0 = a/(2 x);\n\nzzero = qzero^2/(x (x + qzero)^2);\nzplus = -2 (qplus qminus - 2 a^2/(x + qzero))/(x (x + qzero) (x + qminus));\nw1 = a qzero/(x (x + qzero)^2);\n\ntrot = FullSimplify[zplus/(2 hplus)];\ndzero = FullSimplify[zzero/hzero];\n\nexpectedTrot = -(qplus qminus - 2 a^2/(x + qzero))/((x + qplus) (x + qminus) (x + qzero));\nexpectedDzero = qzero^2/(x + qzero)^3;\nprofileExpansion = TrueQ[FullSimplify[trot == expectedTrot && dzero == expectedDzero]];"], "Input"],
 Cell["Trot is the exact rotating version of the static reduction scalar T. Dzero is the fractional correction to Hzero.", "Text"],

 Cell["2. Raw metric, generalized dilaton, and momentum vector", "Section"],
 Cell[BoxData["zPlusFull = hplus + alphaPrime zplus;\nzMinusFull = hminus;\nzZeroFull = hzero + alphaPrime zzero;\nwFull = w0 + alphaPrime w1;\n\nfirstOrder[expr_] := FullSimplify[Normal[Series[expr, {alphaPrime, 0, 1}]]];\ncorrection[expr_] := FullSimplify[Coefficient[firstOrder[expr], alphaPrime, 1]];\n\n(* Coefficients of dt^2, dt sigma3, sigma3^2, and ds(R4)^2. *)\nrawMetricCoefficients = {-1/(zPlusFull zMinusFull), -2 wFull/(zPlusFull zMinusFull), -wFull^2/(zPlusFull zMinusFull), zZeroFull};\nrawMetricCorrection = correction /@ rawMetricCoefficients;\nexpectedMetricCorrection = {\n  2 trot/(hplus hminus),\n  -2 w1/(hplus hminus) + 4 trot w0/(hplus hminus),\n  -2 w0 w1/(hplus hminus) + 2 trot w0^2/(hplus hminus),\n  zzero\n};\nrawMetricReduction = And @@ (TrueQ[FullSimplify[#1 == #2]] & @@@ Transpose[{rawMetricCorrection, expectedMetricCorrection}]);\n\nsigmaAlg = (1/2) Log[zPlusFull/zMinusFull];\nvarphiAlg = (1/4) Log[zZeroFull^2/(zPlusFull zMinusFull)];\nrawDilatonReduction = TrueQ[FullSimplify[correction[varphiAlg] == (dzero - trot)/2]];\n\n(* AAlg is represented by its dt and sigma3 components. *)\naAlg = {1/zPlusFull, wFull/zPlusFull};\naAlgCorrection = correction /@ aAlg;\nexpectedAAlgCorrection = {-2 trot/hplus, (w1 - 2 trot w0)/hplus};\nrawMomentumVectorReduction = And @@ (TrueQ[FullSimplify[#1 == #2]] & @@@ Transpose[{aAlgCorrection, expectedAAlgCorrection}]);"], "Input"],
 Cell["The raw fields are ds5String^2=-(Zplus Zminus)^(-1) Theta^2+Zzero ds(R4)^2, sigmaAlg=(1/2)log(Zplus/Zminus), varphiAlg=(1/4)log[Zzero^2/(Zplus Zminus)], and AAlg=Zplus^(-1)Theta.", "Text"],

 Cell["3. Exact cancellation of the corrected KK radius", "Section"],
 Cell[BoxData["hplusR = 1 + qplus/r^2;\nhminusR = 1 + qminus/r^2;\nhzeroR = 1 + qzero/r^2;\n\n(* The first term comes from the electric part of Fminus and d sigma.\n   The second comes from (d omega0)^2_flat=16 a^2/r^8. *)\ntkk = FullSimplify[-(D[Log[hplusR], r] D[Log[hminusR], r])/(4 hzeroR) + (16 a^2/r^8)/(8 hplusR hminusR hzeroR^2)];\ntkkEqualsTrot = TrueQ[FullSimplify[tkk == (trot /. x -> r^2)]];\n\nsigmaAlgCorrection = correction[sigmaAlg];\ncanonicalSigmaUncorrected = TrueQ[FullSimplify[sigmaAlgCorrection - trot == 0]];"], "Input"],
 Cell["The corrected reduction relation is sigmaAlg=sigmaCanonical+alphaPrime Tkk. Since Tkk=Trot, the canonical STU ratio scalar remains exactly (1/2)log(Hplus/Hminus), without expanding in a.", "Text"],

 Cell["4. Rotation-specific selfdual form", "Section"],
 Cell[BoxData["w1R = a qzero/(r^2 (r^2 + qzero)^2);\nselfDualCoefficient = FullSimplify[D[w1R, r] + 2 w1R/r];\nexpectedSelfDualCoefficient = -4 a qzero/(r (r^2 + qzero)^3);\nrotationSelfDualCoefficient = TrueQ[FullSimplify[selfDualCoefficient == expectedSelfDualCoefficient]];"], "Input"],
 Cell["Hodge-star convention. In this section vol4=-(r^3/8) dr wedge sigma1 wedge sigma2 wedge sigma3, so star4(dr wedge sigma3)=-(r/2) sin(theta) dtheta wedge dphi. Consequently, for omega=W(r)sigma3, d omega+star4 d omega=[W'+2W/r][dr wedge sigma3-(r/2)sin(theta)dtheta wedge dphi]. The leading BMPV one-form is anti-selfdual; the displayed coefficient is the complete first-order departure from anti-selfduality.", "Text"],

 Cell["5. Tail, scalar-constraint, and static checks", "Section"],
 Cell[BoxData["noAsymptoticChargeTail = TrueQ[FullSimplify[Quiet[Limit[x zzero, x -> Infinity]] == 0 && Quiet[Limit[x zplus, x -> Infinity]] == 0 && Quiet[Limit[x w1, x -> Infinity]] == 0]];\n\nClear[varphi, sigma];\nx1 = Exp[2 varphi/3 - sigma];\nx2 = Exp[2 varphi/3 + sigma];\nx3 = Exp[-4 varphi/3];\nstuScalarConstraint = TrueQ[FullSimplify[x1 x2 x3 == 1]];\n\nstaticT = -qplus qminus/((x + qplus) (x + qminus) (x + qzero));\nstaticLimitMatchesKnownMap = TrueQ[FullSimplify[(trot /. a -> 0) == staticT]];"], "Input"],

 Cell["6. Covariant transformations still to be evaluated", "Section"],
 Cell["The complete chain is summarized with explicit formulas in Section 13 of the package-local report_complete/main_new.pdf: corrected winding-vector reduction; Delta1 removing derivatives of field strengths; Delta2 converting the torsionful connection to the torsion-free frame; corrected dualization to C; Ricci-removing and Einstein-frame redefinitions; and the final STU identification. The remaining long local redefinitions are cited there from arXiv:2502.05065. Every correction tensor is evaluated on the two-derivative rotating background.", "Text"],
 Cell["The next machine certificate should use the inverse chain. Starting from the package STU solution, subtract Delta4, undo the Weyl scaling, subtract Delta3, impose corrected dualization, subtract Delta2 and Delta1, undo the corrected KK map, and compare the uplifted metric, dilaton, and gauge-invariant three-form directly with arXiv:2606.31987. At first order the inverse of a local field redefinition is obtained by changing its sign.", "Text"],

 Cell["7. Exact-versus-conditional ledger", "Section"],
 Cell[BoxData["ledger = <|\n  \"ProfileExpansion\" -> profileExpansion,\n  \"RawMetricReduction\" -> rawMetricReduction,\n  \"RawDilatonReduction\" -> rawDilatonReduction,\n  \"RawMomentumVectorReduction\" -> rawMomentumVectorReduction,\n  \"TkkEqualsTrot\" -> tkkEqualsTrot,\n  \"CanonicalSigmaUncorrected\" -> canonicalSigmaUncorrected,\n  \"RotationSelfDualCoefficient\" -> rotationSelfDualCoefficient,\n  \"NoAsymptoticChargeTail\" -> noAsymptoticChargeTail,\n  \"STUScalarConstraint\" -> stuScalarConstraint,\n  \"StaticLimitMatchesKnownMap\" -> staticLimitMatchesKnownMap,\n  \"WindingLorentzCSMap\" -> \"CONDITIONAL: full tensor substitution required\",\n  \"CorrectedDualizationMap\" -> \"CONDITIONAL: full tensor substitution required\",\n  \"FullFiveDimensionalProfileMatch\" -> \"CONDITIONAL: depends on the preceding two checks and radial gauge\"\n|>;\nprovedValues = Values[Take[ledger, 10]];\nfinalPassForProvedSector = And @@ provedValues;\n<|\"Checks\" -> ledger, \"ProvedChecksPassed\" -> Count[provedValues, True], \"ProvedChecksExpected\" -> 10, \"ConditionalChecks\" -> 3, \"FINAL_PASS_PROVED_SECTOR\" -> finalPassForProvedSector|>"], "Input"],
 Cell["Expected result: ten proved checks are True, FINAL_PASS_PROVED_SECTOR is True, and the three unevaluated component checks remain explicitly conditional.", "Text"]
}, WindowTitle -> "Rotating heterotic to STU field map", Saveable -> True]
